1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,566
DappGo existed before this hackathon.

2
00:00:01,566 --> 00:00:05,200
This verifier, its site and every piece of
evidence were built between October 27 and

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:05,700
November 4.

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,100
A finance post goes viral.

5
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:11,500
Thousands repost it.

6
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:12,966
Is it right?

7
00:00:12,966 --> 00:00:18,966
This one has a real number
— and the wrong period.

8
00:00:18,966 --> 00:00:25,700
Numbers like this move money,
and wrong numbers lose it.

9
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,900
And it's not just text.

10
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:30,433
Screenshots,

11
00:00:30,433 --> 00:00:36,000
PDFs, podcasts, videos
— numbers everywhere.

12
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,700
How do you check all of them?

13
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,866
Asking a model directly
gets one in five right.

14
00:00:44,866 --> 00:00:51,000
Give the same model SEC evidence,
and let a program decide:

15
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,700
nine in ten — on held-out
claims, 240 of 266.

16
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:56,866
Here's how.

17
00:00:56,866 --> 00:01:03,900
Meta's Muse Spark reads the post, extracts
each claim and chooses which SEC lookup to

18
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:04,233
run.

19
00:01:04,233 --> 00:01:08,400
Python does the arithmetic
and returns the verdict.

20
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:11,700
The model proposes; the program decides.

21
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,633
Live, on the site.

22
00:01:15,633 --> 00:01:18,700
Paste the post.

23
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:29,900
Muse Spark calls the SEC
tools — you can see each call.

24
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:44,566
Apple's annual revenue was $416
billion; the quarter was $102.5 billion.

25
00:01:44,566 --> 00:01:50,700
Contradicted, with the filing.

26
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:55,166
One cent, six seconds.

27
00:01:55,166 --> 00:02:01,700
And here is the corrected draft.

28
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:09,533
The same checks run in batch from the
command line — text, screenshots through

29
00:02:09,533 --> 00:02:13,933
Muse OCR, audio through
Muse Voice Transcribe.

30
00:02:13,933 --> 00:02:18,800
On saved Threads posts,
the median was 6.8 seconds:

31
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:25,700
a thousand posts would take about 1.9
hours sequentially at that median.

32
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:29,833
Ninety point two percent
on held-out claims.

33
00:02:29,833 --> 00:02:33,366
It wrongly says 'supported' once in 139.

34
00:02:33,366 --> 00:02:36,333
Two cents and ten seconds a claim.

35
00:02:36,333 --> 00:02:41,700
On real posts, coverage is
reported separately from accuracy.

36
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:51,166
Every number, checked against the filing.

37
00:02:51,166 --> 00:02:57,700
hackathon dot dappgo dot com.

